      },
      "text": "7. Conclusion",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14532026143790852,
        "y0": 0.518915404040404,
        "x1": 0.882357843137255,
        "y1": 0.5451098484848484
      },
      "text": "In this paper, we have shown that s(Gn,3) ≤ (1 + o(1))n3 a.a.s., and have additionally made",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.5360227272727273,
        "x1": 0.8823627450980391,
        "y1": 0.5695441919191919
      },
      "text": "the conjecture that s(Gn,3) = (1 + o(1))n4 a.a.s., which is (asymptotically) smallest possible for cubic graphs on n vertices. Resolving this conjecture is an interesting direction for future research.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.5725340909090909,
        "x1": 0.8316813725490195,
        "y1": 0.5964330808080809
      },
      "text": "Another one is to study s(Gn,d) for d ≥ 4—a problem which at present appears challenging.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.5899861111111111,
        "x1": 0.8823594771241831,
        "y1": 0.6721906565656566
      },
      "text": "We considered the following crude technique for upper bounding the Sudoku number of a graph G with chromatic number k. Start with any k-coloring of G using colour classes {1,2,...,k}. Iteratively move vertices from class k to another available class until every remaining vertex has a neighbour in each class i for i = 1,...,k −1. Then the union of classes 1 through k −1 is a Sudoku set for G, and we have the bound",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.6890164141414141,
        "x1": 0.8823529411764706,
        "y1": 0.7340795454545455
      },
      "text": "s(G) ≤ (χ(G) − 1)α(G), (38) where α(G) is the size of the largest independent set in G.",
      "html": null,
